      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip bad\">Hard</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Interval DP</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Split point</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/burst-balloons/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 312</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Burst Balloons</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Choosing the FIRST balloon to burst leaves two halves that still touch, so they are not independent. Choose the LAST balloon k in an open interval (l, r) instead: when it bursts, its neighbours are exactly l and r, and the two sides (l, k) and (k, r) never interact. best[l][r] = max over k of best[l][k] + best[k][r] + v[l]·v[k]·v[r]. O(n<sup>3</sup>) time, O(n<sup>2</sup>) space.</p>\n"
  },
